WEBVTT

00:13.020 --> 00:15.564
- I'm home.
- Oh, Yota!

00:16.523 --> 00:17.733
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:18.275 --> 00:19.109
Huh?

00:19.192 --> 00:22.070
You probably don't wanna be seen
talking to family in front of

00:22.154 --> 00:24.531
your friends.
I embarrassed you, didn't I?

00:26.700 --> 00:28.285
You're at that age... Oh, why'd I call out

00:28.368 --> 00:30.495
- No, it's totally fine.
- to you like that?

00:30.579 --> 00:31.830
I mean you're a teenager.

00:34.833 --> 00:36.043
Thank you for the meal.

00:37.169 --> 00:38.003
Vroom!

00:38.086 --> 00:39.004
Oh, hey there.

00:39.087 --> 00:42.257
Oh, don't hog him so much, Haruto!

00:42.340 --> 00:44.259
Can I possibly finish my food first?

00:44.342 --> 00:45.177
No, now!

00:45.260 --> 00:46.803
You're too loud!

00:46.887 --> 00:47.721
Ahhh.

00:48.889 --> 00:50.515
Would you knock it off, you two!

00:50.599 --> 00:51.433
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:52.059 --> 00:54.352
Don't bother your brother while
he's eating!

00:54.436 --> 00:55.312
WHOOSH

00:57.064 --> 00:59.066
- Oof!
- Do the airplane thing again.

00:59.566 --> 01:00.400
Do it!

01:00.484 --> 01:02.819
- Daddy doesn't have anything left.
- Hey, hey, hey, hey.

01:02.903 --> 01:04.196
- Do it!
- You want me to switch?

01:04.279 --> 01:08.158
No, you don't have to do anything but
eat your dinner. Goodness.

01:08.241 --> 01:09.076
Oh, thank you.

01:12.829 --> 01:13.663
Hey! Hey!

01:15.040 --> 01:15.874
Daddy!

01:24.800 --> 01:25.967
All the noise...

01:26.635 --> 01:29.554
Keeps echoing around in my head non-stop.

01:29.638 --> 01:33.225
- Daddy, Daddy, Daddy!
- Listen to me you two!

01:36.311 --> 01:38.146
I have to make the noise stop.

01:39.356 --> 01:40.649
Or it'll swallow me up.

01:42.818 --> 01:43.652
Don't think.

01:45.654 --> 01:47.405
Don't think about anything.

01:52.536 --> 01:55.372
You see, in my family, I have a
younger sister and brother, and they're

01:55.455 --> 01:57.541
so pigheaded about getting
what they want.

01:57.624 --> 01:58.458
Mm-hm.

01:58.542 --> 02:01.336
The other day, when we were trying to
decide what to have for dinner, as

02:01.419 --> 02:04.631
soon as my sister said "pasta",
my brother simultaneously said "curry!"

02:04.714 --> 02:06.174
Neither of them would give in.

02:06.258 --> 02:07.092
So, I had to-

02:07.175 --> 02:10.053
My younger brother and sister are
still little, so it can get pretty

02:10.137 --> 02:11.638
noisy at home.

02:12.514 --> 02:14.266
Have you been up here all this time?

02:14.349 --> 02:16.476
Yup. Mmm.

02:17.894 --> 02:21.356
You know, daydreaming sounds even better.

02:21.940 --> 02:24.067
The more I think about what he said...

02:25.735 --> 02:28.655
The more everything else he's said
makes so much sense.

02:30.699 --> 02:32.617
But even if I'm right about all of it...

02:33.827 --> 02:36.496
Is it something I should even be getting
involved in?

02:37.998 --> 02:40.542
But if someone insists that they're okay...

02:41.418 --> 02:42.836
Then I should believe them.

02:44.671 --> 02:47.007
And just stay out of their business, right?

04:13.385 --> 04:15.720
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

04:20.141 --> 04:23.937
Loneliness and Solitude

04:24.020 --> 04:25.230
201 YUKI

04:25.313 --> 04:26.856
Koyuki, listen...

04:27.399 --> 04:29.943
Me and your father are divorcing.

04:32.779 --> 04:34.364
- Do you like my apron?
- I knew my parents weren't super

04:34.447 --> 04:35.282
You look adorable, dear.

04:35.365 --> 04:37.617
Lovey-dovey like those couples you
see on TV.

04:38.743 --> 04:41.746
- And that they sometimes argued when
- I'm working myself to the bone all day,

04:41.830 --> 04:42.664
I wasn't around or they thought

04:42.747 --> 04:44.165
- I couldn't hear.
- every day.

04:44.249 --> 04:47.127
I knew all of that. I had no illusions.

04:48.920 --> 04:53.925
But... even then, I was super
close with Mom.

04:54.884 --> 04:57.887
And I felt secure knowing Dad loved me
and was there for me.

04:59.055 --> 05:02.267
I'm pretty sure I was the only
thing keeping them together.

05:04.102 --> 05:06.021
So I thought it would all be okay.

05:07.814 --> 05:09.607
Would Dad be just fine without me?

05:10.358 --> 05:11.276
YUKI

05:11.359 --> 05:12.277
HIKAWA

05:13.069 --> 05:14.988
Like I never even mattered to him?

05:20.201 --> 05:22.454
Ew, her water bottle is so lame,
isn't it?

05:22.537 --> 05:24.622
Oh my gosh, stop, Manatsu!

05:26.291 --> 05:27.709
I didn't fit in at school.

05:28.460 --> 05:32.297
I felt like I didn't belong anywhere,
really, no matter where I was.

05:33.465 --> 05:37.969
Tell me, Koyun, what it is you don't
like about Igarashi?

05:38.053 --> 05:39.220
There's probably a lot.

05:40.430 --> 05:43.808
I felt so isolated with no one I
could share my feelings with.

05:44.893 --> 05:45.810
And this fear...

05:47.062 --> 05:50.440
This voice that wouldn't leave me
alone said, "no one cares whether

05:50.523 --> 05:52.817
you're around or not."

05:53.902 --> 05:56.738
Eventually, I started to believe it.

05:57.489 --> 05:59.074
And it broke my heart.

06:01.409 --> 06:03.828
CLUB WITHDRAWAL FORM

06:09.417 --> 06:10.877
Back then, I...

06:12.170 --> 06:14.422
I felt lonelier when I was with someone.

06:19.928 --> 06:21.930
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

06:22.430 --> 06:25.100
WHEW... WHEW...

06:25.183 --> 06:27.602
Our circumstances are completely
different.

06:27.685 --> 06:30.188
- Yota isn't me.
- What time is your club over today?

06:30.271 --> 06:34.567
What feels right for me may be completely
different than what's right for him.

06:35.860 --> 06:38.488
Still... I know how he feels.

06:39.280 --> 06:40.615
- Send!
- SEND

06:41.324 --> 06:42.367
That loneliness...

06:43.326 --> 06:46.955
The kind you experience when you're
with others yet still feel so alone.

06:48.248 --> 06:49.082
Hm?

06:50.708 --> 06:51.876
Oh, Koyun.

06:51.960 --> 06:53.878
- KOYUKI: ABOUT WHAT TIME DOES YOUR CLUB
- Probably...

06:53.962 --> 06:57.424
- END TODAY? PROBABLY... A...
- Around when we're all-

06:57.507 --> 06:58.550
Hm?

07:00.385 --> 07:02.720
Agh! Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, your
phone!

07:03.388 --> 07:05.473
Ah! Whew! Close one.

07:06.474 --> 07:09.519
ABOUT WHAT TIME DOES YOUR CLUB END TODAY?
PROBABLY AN UPRISING

07:09.602 --> 07:11.604
Oh, uh, sorry. I appreciate it.

07:13.189 --> 07:14.107
I saw it.

07:16.609 --> 07:18.528
Probably an uprising.

07:19.362 --> 07:20.697
What does this mean?

07:22.240 --> 07:23.992
- Huh?
- Probably around when we're all leaving.

07:24.075 --> 07:25.285
Sorry, typo! LOL

07:26.536 --> 07:27.704
- Whew!
- HEH

07:28.204 --> 07:30.540
BLAZING CHINESE GYOSHO

07:31.332 --> 07:34.544
And then, before I could fix it,
I dropped my phone and ended up

07:34.627 --> 07:36.129
sending it instead.

07:37.505 --> 07:39.841
I was like, oh my gosh, that's a
heck of a typo.

07:39.924 --> 07:40.925
What can I say?

07:44.095 --> 07:44.929
You grandpa.

07:45.013 --> 07:47.265
Oh, so I've gone from "dad" to "grandpa"
now.

07:50.935 --> 07:52.520
Sorry for dragging you along.

07:52.604 --> 07:53.646
It's fine.

07:57.192 --> 07:58.026
Mm.

07:59.569 --> 08:00.403
Um...

08:01.112 --> 08:01.946
So my...

08:03.239 --> 08:04.449
My parents are divorced.

08:05.450 --> 08:06.284
Huh?

08:09.704 --> 08:11.664
I'm often alone when I get home.

08:13.249 --> 08:15.919
So if you're free, even if it's just
once in a while...

08:18.129 --> 08:21.674
I'd really like it if we could maybe hang
out after school.

08:26.221 --> 08:27.055
It'd be nice.

08:31.351 --> 08:32.894
You're such a kind person.

08:33.728 --> 08:35.146
Huh? N- No way!

08:35.230 --> 08:37.815
I'm judgy and moody and get mad
super easily.

08:37.899 --> 08:39.234
No you're not.

08:42.320 --> 08:43.238
You're very kind.

08:43.947 --> 08:45.073
At least to me.

08:46.574 --> 08:47.408
Hm.

08:49.160 --> 08:49.994
Sorry.

08:51.412 --> 08:54.499
But can I share with you for just a sec?

08:55.583 --> 08:56.417
Mm-hm.

09:03.591 --> 09:08.012
A little after my mom died, Dad just, he
suddenly got super busy.

09:08.721 --> 09:11.224
He couldn't make it to any school events.

09:12.350 --> 09:14.769
NOTICE OF CLASS OBSERVATION

09:15.395 --> 09:19.148
I tried not to let it bother me too much
on Bring Your Parent to Class days

09:19.232 --> 09:20.275
FIDGETY

09:24.696 --> 09:25.530
And then...

09:26.155 --> 09:28.241
Hi Yota, it's nice to meet you.

09:28.992 --> 09:30.159
You're so tall.

09:30.660 --> 09:31.869
Yota, meet Akari.

09:32.996 --> 09:36.499
Dad introduced me to the woman I now call
Mom.

09:37.709 --> 09:39.961
Uh. Sorry! He's just shy around people.

09:40.044 --> 09:41.671
Yota, c'mon she doesn't bite.

09:41.754 --> 09:43.798
Uh. Um, can we, um...

09:44.757 --> 09:48.052
And Mom, well, she's been super nice
to me.

09:55.435 --> 09:56.269
But...

09:58.062 --> 10:00.565
Akari! I got paternity leave!

10:01.107 --> 10:02.066
Ah, really!

10:02.150 --> 10:03.693
- Mm-hm!
- I'm so happy.

10:03.776 --> 10:06.029
- They finally approved it.
- Thank goodness.

10:06.112 --> 10:07.155
Sometimes I wonder.

10:08.323 --> 10:09.157
Ooh, yummy!

10:09.240 --> 10:11.409
- See? I knew you'd like it.
- Is it good?

10:11.492 --> 10:13.494
If I even exist to them.

10:15.163 --> 10:21.419
I feel like I'm the only one in the
family who just doesn't belong.

10:24.380 --> 10:26.299
I know I'm being really self-centered.

10:27.300 --> 10:29.552
But the thought won't leave me alone.

10:31.638 --> 10:32.889
I'm just running from it.

10:39.228 --> 10:43.441
Yota, you shouldn't beat yourself
up for how you feel or what you think.

10:44.233 --> 10:46.152
I know how he feels so much it hurts.

10:47.320 --> 10:49.614
Don't judge yourself for feeling what
you feel.

10:49.697 --> 10:51.407
It will just makes you feel worse.

10:52.742 --> 10:55.078
Because the more you judge and blame
yourself...

10:55.787 --> 10:58.915
You just hate yourself that much
more, right?

10:59.415 --> 11:02.627
Even if you run away from your
circumstances, you can't run away

11:02.710 --> 11:03.628
from yourself.

11:06.089 --> 11:07.799
You're amazing. You know that?

11:08.299 --> 11:09.342
Huh?

11:10.176 --> 11:11.094
You really see me.

11:22.522 --> 11:23.898
Huh? Wait, are you crying?

11:25.066 --> 11:25.900
Oh.

11:25.983 --> 11:27.402
- SHARP
- Don't worry about it.

11:27.485 --> 11:31.322
It's like a glitch that happens whenever
emotions get too big for me to process.

11:31.406 --> 11:33.116
- What?
- Yeah, happens all the time.

11:33.199 --> 11:34.242
Huh?

11:35.618 --> 11:37.912
I was jealous of Yota all this time.

11:38.496 --> 11:42.333
He was a different gender, height, had a
very different personality from me.

11:43.835 --> 11:47.839
I figured his kindness was a byproduct of
his strength and composure.

11:47.922 --> 11:48.840
Just who he was.

11:50.717 --> 11:53.302
But it came from pushing things down
or giving up.

11:54.762 --> 11:57.223
And that's... That's so sad.

11:59.809 --> 12:00.643
Yota.

12:01.519 --> 12:03.104
You don't have to be nice all the time.

12:03.187 --> 12:04.230
Hm?

12:05.273 --> 12:07.483
It's okay to feel what you wanna feel.

12:13.781 --> 12:15.575
SIGH

12:15.658 --> 12:16.492
Hm?

12:17.243 --> 12:18.661
Thanks for letting me vent.

12:19.370 --> 12:21.122
Sorry, I hope I wasn't too weird.

12:21.706 --> 12:23.833
Not at all. You're fine.

12:25.334 --> 12:28.212
All that stuff I told you, I've never
shared with anyone.

12:29.005 --> 12:31.924
To be honest, I wouldn't even have
shared this with Minato.

12:32.008 --> 12:33.009
I'm surprised.

12:33.801 --> 12:35.803
You really care for Amamiya, don't you?

12:37.346 --> 12:38.181
No way.

12:38.890 --> 12:39.724
Okay, sure.

12:41.434 --> 12:44.479
If you're fine with me, then I'm happy to
listen.

12:45.855 --> 12:51.986
If you hold it in too much, then your
heart will just get all covered in soot.

12:52.528 --> 12:53.404
- In soot?
- Mm-hm.

12:53.488 --> 12:54.322
In soot.

12:55.698 --> 12:57.784
As it builds up, it makes everything
harder.

12:57.867 --> 13:00.244
And you can't see things clearly anymore.

13:03.706 --> 13:04.540
Hmm.

13:04.624 --> 13:05.458
I see.

13:05.958 --> 13:07.084
Sounds about right.

13:08.878 --> 13:09.712
Mmm.

13:11.547 --> 13:12.381
Uhh.

13:14.175 --> 13:15.009
Mmm.

13:19.472 --> 13:20.389
What should I do?

13:20.890 --> 13:21.808
Huh?

13:23.351 --> 13:24.185
Koyun.

13:24.894 --> 13:25.728
I, um...

13:35.571 --> 13:36.405
Well, I...

13:38.658 --> 13:39.534
You see...

13:40.409 --> 13:41.244
I like...

13:43.704 --> 13:44.539
Huh?

13:53.798 --> 13:54.757
You see...

13:54.841 --> 13:55.925
I like...

13:58.719 --> 13:59.554
Huh?

14:02.557 --> 14:04.559
I like... Miki.

14:12.441 --> 14:14.277
What? What? What?

14:14.360 --> 14:15.903
PANIC

14:15.987 --> 14:17.572
FLUSTER FLUSTER

14:18.072 --> 14:19.031
What?

14:24.203 --> 14:25.037
Yeah, it's both.

14:27.331 --> 14:28.207
No way.

14:29.250 --> 14:30.751
I- I didn't see this coming!

14:30.835 --> 14:32.753
You seem so chill all the time!

14:33.588 --> 14:36.007
Oh, well, yeah, I'm really not.

14:36.924 --> 14:40.428
If you haven't noticed, I'm always
a total mess whenever Miki's around.

14:40.511 --> 14:41.554
Really?

14:42.179 --> 14:43.431
But I've never seen...

14:49.145 --> 14:49.979
Never mind.

14:50.897 --> 14:53.816
Minato figured it out a long time ago.

14:54.358 --> 14:57.236
IT'S NOT THE CASE
WAIT, WAIT

14:57.320 --> 15:00.323
- He must feel embarrassed.
- I keep denying it cause it annoys me.

15:00.406 --> 15:02.325
Whoa. What Is this feeling?

15:02.950 --> 15:04.201
I'm super happy!

15:06.078 --> 15:08.581
Maybe I don't even know who the real me
is.

15:08.664 --> 15:11.459
Or what my real feelings even are.

15:11.542 --> 15:12.418
GRR!

15:12.501 --> 15:15.296
Like, don't fantasize about who
you think I am and then get mad when

15:15.379 --> 15:18.883
Like, don't fantasize about who
you think I am and then get mad when

15:18.966 --> 15:19.800
Well, Miki...

15:19.884 --> 15:21.844
There's someone who likes you
just the way you are.

15:21.928 --> 15:23.638
And... He's such a wonderful person.

15:28.225 --> 15:29.977
(BURSTING-WITH-JOY DANCE)

15:30.061 --> 15:34.065
- You wanna date Miki, huh?
- Koyun, why are you suddenly acting weird?

15:34.148 --> 15:34.982
So, Yota.

15:35.066 --> 15:35.900
GIDDY

15:35.983 --> 15:37.276
Sorry, I'm just happy.

15:37.360 --> 15:38.486
Oh, but...

15:43.199 --> 15:44.659
How does Miki feel about him?

15:46.911 --> 15:48.871
I haven't thought that far.

15:50.373 --> 15:53.000
Honestly, I don't really plan
on telling her.

15:54.460 --> 15:55.962
I just like her, is all.

15:56.462 --> 15:57.755
Let's leave it at that.

15:58.965 --> 16:00.007
Her friendship...

16:00.091 --> 16:01.467
Means the world to me.

16:03.135 --> 16:06.389
And I know she doesn't see me the
same way, and honestly I'm okay

16:06.472 --> 16:07.723
with that.

16:09.141 --> 16:09.976
But then...

16:11.227 --> 16:14.897
Keeping this secret, I'm starting to
feel like I'm deceiving her

16:15.982 --> 16:19.026
I feel like I should apologize for liking
her.

16:19.527 --> 16:20.528
GASP

16:20.611 --> 16:22.321
I told you, don't blame yourself!

16:22.405 --> 16:23.406
The soot!

16:27.493 --> 16:29.578
Let's keep this conversation between us.

16:29.662 --> 16:30.788
I won't say a word.

16:31.288 --> 16:33.040
I'm really rooting for you, Yota.

16:33.541 --> 16:35.418
Just don't be too obvious around her.

16:36.877 --> 16:37.712
I'll try.

16:39.839 --> 16:40.673
Hm.

16:41.757 --> 16:42.800
It feels like a thumb.

16:42.883 --> 16:43.718
It's my pinky.

16:45.469 --> 16:49.265
You know, I'm really glad I became
friends with you.

16:53.477 --> 16:54.311
I am too.

16:57.440 --> 16:58.482
Yota! Welcome back!

16:59.650 --> 17:00.484
I'm home.

17:01.402 --> 17:02.820
STARE

17:03.320 --> 17:05.072
Did you stop somewhere on your way?

17:05.156 --> 17:05.990
EEK

17:06.073 --> 17:07.324
Did I come home too late?

17:08.492 --> 17:10.202
Yeah. With a friend.

17:10.703 --> 17:11.829
Oh, I knew it!

17:12.580 --> 17:16.292
You looked cheerful, so I thought maybe
something good might've happened.

17:17.334 --> 17:18.169
Huh?

17:18.669 --> 17:20.171
- Big brother!
- Big brother!

17:20.254 --> 17:21.547
Oh, come on!

17:22.798 --> 17:24.508
Can we dry our hair first, please?

17:24.592 --> 17:25.468
My goodness.

17:25.968 --> 17:27.344
But no, it's not fair.

17:27.428 --> 17:29.597
You always go straight to your room.

17:29.680 --> 17:30.723
Yeah.

17:30.806 --> 17:32.099
That's why we came to get you!

17:32.183 --> 17:33.350
Big bro, big bro, big bro.

17:33.434 --> 17:35.186
Go ahead and dry your hair. I'll wait
for you.

17:35.269 --> 17:36.103
Let's play!

17:36.187 --> 17:37.021
- Really?
- Really?

17:37.104 --> 17:38.022
Yeah!

17:38.105 --> 17:38.939
- Yay!
- Yay!

17:39.023 --> 17:39.857
- Ah!
- Jeez.

17:41.734 --> 17:42.985
Oh. Yota.

17:43.069 --> 17:44.361
There's ice cream in the freezer.

17:44.445 --> 17:45.488
The fancy kind.

17:46.197 --> 17:48.240
Only after he finishes his dinner.

17:48.324 --> 17:50.242
HMPH!

17:52.536 --> 17:56.791
Without even trying, everyone's
kindness is warming my heart.

17:59.668 --> 18:03.130
Why did I ever believe I didn't belong
here?

18:04.548 --> 18:05.382
Soot.

18:07.635 --> 18:08.719
So that's it.

18:09.637 --> 18:11.847
I never knew what it was before.

18:14.391 --> 18:16.519
I can't even remember the last time...

18:18.312 --> 18:19.563
I had a night this quiet.

18:23.984 --> 18:25.653
Did you sleep well last night?

18:25.736 --> 18:27.113
Yeah, very well.

18:27.738 --> 18:28.572
Good.

18:30.116 --> 18:30.950
What the...

18:31.992 --> 18:33.911
Oh, hey. You get something to drink?

18:33.994 --> 18:35.079
Uh-huh.

18:35.579 --> 18:36.413
Hey, Amamiya.

18:37.081 --> 18:37.957
It's been awhile.

18:39.750 --> 18:40.876
Uh, yeah, it sure has.

18:42.419 --> 18:43.254
Oh, great!

18:43.337 --> 18:44.171
- Hm?
- Hm?

18:44.255 --> 18:46.340
- The three of you are here together!
- Huh?

18:46.423 --> 18:49.593
- Jeez, she's got so many snacks.
- Jeez, she's got so many snacks.

18:49.677 --> 18:51.762
Having bread from the school store for
lunch too?

18:51.846 --> 18:53.097
Yeah, silly me.

18:53.180 --> 18:55.850
I forgot to grab my lunch on the
way out this morning.

18:55.933 --> 18:56.851
That's not good.

18:56.934 --> 18:57.893
Wait!

18:57.977 --> 18:58.936
There were buns left?

18:59.019 --> 19:00.521
Yeah. You can have it.

19:00.604 --> 19:02.231
No, I'll pay for it.

19:02.314 --> 19:03.149
How much?

19:04.024 --> 19:05.568
UNEASY

19:09.155 --> 19:09.989
Hmm.

19:11.532 --> 19:13.033
It's fine. You can have it.

19:13.117 --> 19:15.161
No, I wanna pay for it.

19:15.244 --> 19:16.120
Fine, ten yen.

19:16.203 --> 19:17.121
That can't be right.

19:17.204 --> 19:18.330
Let's trade one.

19:19.623 --> 19:20.457
Mm?

19:21.167 --> 19:22.042
Amamiya.

19:23.586 --> 19:25.588
So, what'd you do over winter break?

19:26.589 --> 19:28.048
She initiated a conversation.

19:29.175 --> 19:32.678
Just, uh, uh. mostly doing club
activities.

19:33.637 --> 19:36.015
And sometimes I hung out with my
classmates.

19:36.599 --> 19:38.184
And I walked my, uh, dog.

19:39.018 --> 19:39.852
A dog?

19:39.935 --> 19:41.103
FUZZY

19:42.146 --> 19:42.980
And I, uh...

19:44.148 --> 19:45.357
When I talk to her...

19:46.400 --> 19:49.320
No matter how hard I try, I can never say
the right thing.

19:50.362 --> 19:52.323
I don't know what to do.

19:53.657 --> 19:55.910
- By the way...
- Hm?

19:55.993 --> 19:58.078
- I'd really love to know the name.
- Huh?

19:58.162 --> 19:59.622
- My name?
- No.

19:59.705 --> 20:01.916
- Your dog's.
- Oh.

20:03.042 --> 20:04.960
Because I'm pretty sure you're Minato.

20:08.297 --> 20:09.131
It's Ponta.

20:10.007 --> 20:10.841
Huh?

20:11.342 --> 20:12.468
Oh, no, I meant the dog!

20:12.551 --> 20:14.553
- PONTA AMAMIYA PONTA
- I'm not Ponta, clearly!

20:14.637 --> 20:16.138
Wait, what am I even saying?

20:16.889 --> 20:18.724
- HEH
- Huh?

20:21.268 --> 20:22.269
Wow, I guess you're...

20:23.312 --> 20:24.939
- Ponta!
- Yeah, yeah.

20:25.439 --> 20:27.024
Go ahead, laugh it up.

20:28.317 --> 20:29.151
Sorry.

20:30.694 --> 20:33.280
Sweet red beans are clearly your
favorite, huh?

20:33.781 --> 20:34.990
Heck, yeah!

20:35.074 --> 20:36.617
I can't get enough of 'em!

20:36.700 --> 20:37.534
Right, Koyu-

20:38.035 --> 20:39.119
Is Ponta doing well?

20:39.620 --> 20:40.454
- Mm-hm.
- Wait,

20:40.537 --> 20:41.997
I take tons of pictures.

20:42.081 --> 20:44.375
- Ooh, I wanna see.
- Well, what's going on here?

20:44.458 --> 20:46.085
- Am I...
- Koyun...

20:48.837 --> 20:50.339
- Wha-
- What the heck?

20:51.548 --> 20:54.051
I've got lots of pent-up energy.

20:54.134 --> 20:55.261
What'd ya do that for?

20:55.344 --> 20:56.303
You scare me.

20:59.098 --> 20:59.932
Jeez.

21:00.015 --> 21:01.767
- I'm sorry.
- You're being too good of a wing

21:01.850 --> 21:03.310
- Eh, it's fine.
- woman there.

21:04.436 --> 21:05.271
Oh, gosh. Sorry.

21:05.354 --> 21:06.730
SMILE GUARD SMILE GUARD ALPHA

21:06.814 --> 21:08.774
Hey, I told you, stop making that face!

21:10.025 --> 21:10.859
Sorry, sorry.

21:11.610 --> 21:12.945
Huh? What's this?

21:13.612 --> 21:14.905
Are those two...

21:16.615 --> 21:20.202
- Their chemistry is off the charts!
- Their chemistry is off the charts!

21:20.744 --> 21:22.162
Well, I'm gonna go now.

21:22.663 --> 21:23.956
Eating in again?

21:25.165 --> 21:26.000
Yeah.

21:26.500 --> 21:27.334
Eating in where?

21:27.418 --> 21:28.585
THE SCHOOL NURSE NORIKO

21:28.669 --> 21:30.921
I said the nurse's office isn't
a food court!

21:31.839 --> 21:32.673
Well, see ya.

21:33.757 --> 21:34.591
Yeah, later!

21:39.388 --> 21:41.807
I can't totally say for sure yet,
but two of my favorite people in

21:41.890 --> 21:42.725
the whole world might be falling for each
other.

21:42.808 --> 21:45.227
The whole world might be falling for each
other.

21:47.021 --> 21:50.733
Oh my gosh, why does that make me so
freaking excited?!

21:52.026 --> 21:55.446
Hey, look, I- I know it's still a
long way off, but d'you guys wanna

21:55.529 --> 21:58.324
study together for final exams again?

22:03.120 --> 22:03.954
- Sure.
- Sure.

22:04.038 --> 22:04.872
Awesome!

22:05.831 --> 22:08.584
And I'll be playing the role of Cupid
for them!

22:11.170 --> 22:14.048
- Wait, is that Miki?
- Alright, I'm gonna study my butt off!

22:14.131 --> 22:17.843
The guys she's with.
That's clearly Hino and Amamiya, right?

22:19.803 --> 22:23.807
Guys, has Miki always been like that?
